21","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#cacheruntime-pods-cannot-generate-curvine-config","content":"CacheRuntime pods cannot generate Curvine config","locale":"en"},"24":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-22","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#mountufs-fails","content":"MountUFS fails","locale":"en"},"25":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-23","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#fuse-mount-is-missing","content":"FUSE mount is missing","locale":"en"},"26":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-24","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#dataload-job-starts-but-fails","content":"DataLoad job starts but fails","locale":"en"},"27":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-25","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","content":"Fluid exposes a Kubernetes `Dataset` to application pods. Curvine can be used as the cache runtime behind that Dataset, or as an existing storage cluster that Fluid only mounts.","locale":"en"},"28":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-26","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","content":"For new Fluid deployments, start with **CacheRuntime**. It lets Fluid create Curvine master, worker, and FUSE client pods, and it is the path that supports CacheRuntime data operations such as `DataLoad`.","locale":"en"},"29":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-27","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#choose-an-integration-mode","content":"| Mode         | Use it when                                                     | What Fluid starts                             | Main resources                                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| CacheRuntime | You want Fluid to manage a Curvine cache cluster in Kubernetes. | Curvine master, worker, and client/FUSE pods. | `CacheRuntimeClass`, `Dataset`, `CacheRuntime` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"30":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-28","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#choose-an-integration-mode","content":"| Mode        | Use it when                                                                        | What Fluid starts          | Main resources                                 |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| ThinRuntime | You already have a Curvine cluster and only need Fluid to mount it into workloads. | Curvine FUSE runtime only. | `ThinRuntimeProfile`, `Dataset`, `ThinRuntime` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"31":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-29","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#choose-an-integration-mode","content":"CacheRuntime is the recommended mode for most users. ThinRuntime is useful when Curvine is operated outside Fluid.","locale":"en"},"32":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-30","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#files-and-references","content":"The Curvine Fluid materials live in the Curvine source tree:","locale":"en"},"33":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integratio