rl":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#start-the-local-cluster","content":"If you compiled Curvine inside a Docker container, run it in the same environment unless you are sure the host runtime dependencies match the build environment.","locale":"en"},"1402":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-15","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#logs-and-pid-files","content":"Service lifecycle management goes through `bin/launch-process.sh`.","locale":"en"},"1403":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-16","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#logs-and-pid-files","content":"Logs are written to `logs/master.out`, `logs/worker.out`, and `logs/fuse.out`","locale":"en"},"1404":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-17","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#logs-and-pid-files","content":"PID files are written at the Curvine home directory root as `master.pid`, `worker.pid`, and `fuse.pid`","locale":"en"},"1405":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-18","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#verify-status","content":"Check the cluster summary:","locale":"en"},"1406":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-19","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#verify-status","content":"Check that FUSE is mounted:","locale":"en"},"1407":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-20","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#web-endpoints","content":"Master web endpoint: `http://<host>:9000`","locale":"en"},"1408":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-21","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#web-endpoints","content":"Worker web endpoint: `http://<host>:9001`","locale":"en"},"1409":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-22","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#web-endpoints","content":"If you run inside Docker, use `--network host` or map at least `8995`, `8996`, `8997`, `9000`, and `9001`. If you need browser access to the FUSE web endpoint as well, include `9002`.","locale":"en"},"1410":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-23","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#alternative-helper-script","content":"The distribution also includes `bin/local-cluster.sh`, which manages only Master and Worker:","locale":"en"},"1411":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode-24","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Standalone-Mode#alternative-helper-script","content":"Use `restart-all.sh` when you want FUSE mounted as part of the local setup. Use `local-cluster.sh` when you only need the server-side processes.","locale":"en"},"1412":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster","type":"page","content":"Deploy Curvine Cluster","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Deploy Curvine Cluster"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster","locale":"en"},"1413":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","type":"page","content":"Deployment Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Deployment Overview"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","locale":"en"},"1414":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Component Roles","locale":"en"},"1415":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#relationship-between-curvine-master-curvine-worker-and-curvine-fuse","content":"Relationship between curvine master, curvine worker, and curvine fuse","locale":"en"},"1416":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#curvine-fuse-use-cases","content":"curvine fuse Use Cases","locale":"en"},"1417":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","content":"Before deploying a cluster, you need to understand the roles of each Curvine component and their interaction patterns. The following diagram shows the typical deployment architecture of Curvine, divided into three layers from top to bottom:","locale":"en"},"1418":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","content":"**Application Layer**: Includes curvine-fuse, applications accessed via SDK, CLI management tools, etc. For details, refer to Access Methods.","locale":"en"},"1419":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","content":"**Curvine Cluster Service Layer**: Consists of **curvine-master** (can be multiple nodes for HA, forming a Raft group) and **curvine-worker** nodes forming the Curvine cluster.","locale":"en"},"1420":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","content":"**UFS Cluster**: As the underlying storage backend, connected to the Curvine cluster through mounting, such as S3, HDFS, and other clusters.","locale":"en"},"1421":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"**Master nodes** (can be multiple for high availability): Responsible for metadata management, worker node coordination, and load balancing","locale":"en"},"1422":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Deployed as a Raft group (one leader, multiple followers); clients talk to the current leader","locale":"en"},"1423":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Maintains file system metadata (directory structure, file locations, etc.)","locale":"en"},"1424":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Manages worker node registration and health checks","locale":"en"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Handles client metadata requests","locale":"en"},"1426":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Uses Raft consensus algorithm to ensure metadata consistency","locale":"en"},"1427":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"**Worker Node**: Responsible for data storage and processing","locale":"en"},"1428":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Stores actual data blocks (supports memory, SSD, HDD multi-level caching)","locale":"en"},"1429":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Handles data read/write requests","locale":"en"},"1430":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Periodically sends heartbeats to Master","locale":"en"},"1431":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"Supports multi-replica data storage","locale":"en"},"1432":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"**FUSE Interface**: Provides POSIX file system interface, mounting distributed cache as local file system","locale":"en"},"1433":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"**S3 Gateway**: Provides S3-compatible object storage interface, supporting S3 API","locale":"en"},"1434":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#component-roles","content":"**Client Library**: Provides multi-language APIs, communicating with Master and Worker nodes via RPC","locale":"en"},"1435":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#relationship-between-curvine-master-curvine-worker-and-curvine-fuse","content":"Master is deployed as **multiple nodes** (Raft group). Clients and FUSE communicate with the current master leader; the diagram below shows the logical roles.","locale":"en"},"1436":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-22","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#curvine-fuse-use-cases","content":"When you need to enable existing applications to access Curvine distributed cache without modification, FUSE can be used to mount Curvine as a local file system.","locale":"en"},"1437":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-23","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#curvine-fuse-use-cases","content":"Default mount points","locale":"en"},"1438":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture-24","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview/Deployment-Architecture#curvine-fuse-use-cases","content":"/curvine-fuse","locale":"en"},"1439":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","type":"page","content":"Deployment Overview","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Deployment Overview"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","locale":"en"},"1440":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#deployment-sequence","content":"Deployment Sequence","locale":"en"},"1441":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#documentation-boundaries","content":"Documentation Boundaries","locale":"en"},"1442":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#production-changes","content":"Production Changes","locale":"en"},"1443":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-3","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","content":"This chapter separates cluster installation from optional services. Deploy and\nverify the Curvine Master and Workers first. Add the Transfer service only when\nLoad or Export jobs should run outside the Master process.","locale":"en"},"1444":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-4","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#deployment-sequence","content":"Choose a cluster form.","locale":"en"},"1445":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-5","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#deployment-sequence","content":"Use Quick Start for a local evaluation.","locale":"en"},"1446":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-6","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#deployment-sequence","content":"Use Standalone Mode for a\nsingle-host cluster.","locale":"en"},"1447":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-7","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#deployment-sequence","content":"Use bare metal\nor Kubernetes\nfor a distributed cluster.","locale":"en"},"1448":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-8","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#deployment-sequence","content":"Verify that Master and Worker processes are healthy and that required UFS\nmounts can be listed with `cv mount --check`.","locale":"en"},"1449":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-9","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#deployment-sequence","content":"If the cluster needs independent Load and Export scheduling, deploy the\nTransfer Service.","locale":"en"},"1450":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-10","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#deployment-sequence","content":"Enable Transfer only in the clients that should use it. Existing clients can\ncontinue to use the legacy Master job path during a staged rollout.","locale":"en"},"1451":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-11","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#documentation-boundaries","content":"Cluster deployment pages describe Master, Worker, storage, and networking.","locale":"en"},"1452":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-12","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#documentation-boundaries","content":"Transfer pages describe the independent scheduler, its state store, and\nclient routing.","locale":"en"},"1453":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-13","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#documentation-boundaries","content":"The configuration reference\nis the single source for configuration defaults. Deployment pages show only\nthe settings required for each topology.","locale":"en"},"1454":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview-14","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deployment-Overview#production-changes","content":"Treat upgrades as a separate operation. Verify version compatibility and\nconfiguration changes in a non-production cluster before changing the running\ncluster. For Transfer, use a shared MySQL store before running more than one\ninstance.","locale":"en"},"1455":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","type":"page","content":"Deploy Transfer on Bare Metal","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Transfer Service"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","locale":"en"},"1456":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#prepare-the-service-configuration","content":"Prepare the Service Configuration","locale":"en"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#start-and-stop","content":"Start and Stop","locale":"en"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#run-under-systemd","content":"Run Under systemd","locale":"en"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-3","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#verify","content":"Verify","locale":"en"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-4","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#high-availability","content":"High Availability","locale":"en"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-5","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","content":"This guide deploys one independent Transfer process next to an existing\nCurvine cluster. Master and Worker processes must already be running and must\ncome from a version that supports Transfer tasks.","locale":"en"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-6","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#prepare-the-service-configuration","content":"Start with the cluster configuration that already contains the Master addresses\nand create a Transfer-specific copy. The `[transfer]` section below is the only\nnew section required for a single-instance SQLite deployment.","locale":"en"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-7","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#prepare-the-service-configuration","content":"Create the store directory with the same operating-system user that runs the\nservice. The SQLite database must live on persistent local or block storage.\nDo not put it on a shared filesystem or run a second Transfer process against\nit.","locale":"en"},"1464":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-8","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#start-and-stop","content":"The distribution includes a Transfer launcher. It sources `curvine-env.sh`,\nwrites `logs/transfer.out`, and manages `transfer.pid`.","locale":"en"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-9","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#run-under-systemd","content":"Use the bundled launcher so that the service receives the normal Curvine shell\nenvironment. Save the following as `/etc/systemd/system/curvine-transfer.service`.","locale":"en"},"1466":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-10","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#verify","content":"The client address must be reachable from every CLI user and from every Worker\nthat may execute a Transfer task.","locale":"en"},"1467":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal-11","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Bare-Metal#high-availability","content":"For multiple Transfer processes, replace the SQLite URL with one shared MySQL\n`store_url`. Give every process a unique reachable address and publish one\nstable client endpoint through a load balancer or DNS name. Do not use multiple\nindependent SQLite databases as failover targets.","locale":"en"},"1468":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","type":"page","content":"Deploy Transfer on Kubernetes","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Transfer Service"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","locale":"en"},"1469":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"1470":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#sqlite-single-replica-manifest","content":"SQLite Single-Replica Manifest","locale":"en"},"1471":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#configure-clients","content":"Configure Clients","locale":"en"},"1472":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-3","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#mysql-multi-replica-deployment","content":"MySQL Multi-Replica Deployment","locale":"en"},"1473":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-4","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","content":"Deploy Transfer separately from the Master and Worker workloads. The current\nCurvine Helm chart does not create this service, so use a dedicated manifest.\nThe SQLite manifest below is intentionally a single replica with a dedicated\nRWO volume.","locale":"en"},"1474":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-5","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#prerequisites","content":"An existing Curvine Master and Worker deployment in the namespace.","locale":"en"},"1475":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-6","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#prerequisites","content":"A ConfigMap containing the existing `curvine-cluster.toml` with the key name\nshown below. Replace `curvine-cluster-config` if your deployment uses a\ndifferent name.","locale":"en"},"1476":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-7","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#prerequisites","content":"A default `StorageClass` that supports `ReadWriteOnce` volumes, or a\n`storageClassName` added to the PVC.","locale":"en"},"1477":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-8","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#prerequisites","content":"An image version that matches the Master and Worker version.","locale":"en"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-9","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#sqlite-single-replica-manifest","content":"Save this as `transfer-sqlite.yaml`. Replace the image and namespace to match\nyour cluster.","locale":"en"},"1479":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-10","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#sqlite-single-replica-manifest","content":"Mount only the generated `curvine-cluster.toml` file into the main container.\nMounting an `emptyDir` over the whole `/app/curvine/conf` directory hides the\nimage's `curvine-env.sh` and breaks bundled client scripts.","locale":"en"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-11","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#sqlite-single-replica-manifest","content":"Apply and verify the service:","locale":"en"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-12","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#configure-clients","content":"For clients inside the Kubernetes cluster, use the Service DNS name:","locale":"en"},"1482":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-13","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#configure-clients","content":"For a client outside the cluster, publish an address that it can reach. A\n`.svc.cluster.local` address is only valid from the cluster network.","locale":"en"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes-14","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Kubernetes#mysql-multi-replica-deployment","content":"To run more than one Transfer replica, use a shared MySQL `store_url` supplied\nthrough a Secret, remove the SQLite PVC, and expose all replicas through the\nsame ClusterIP Service. All replicas must use the same database and compatible\nimage version. Do not scale the SQLite Deployment above one replica.","locale":"en"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","type":"page","content":"Transfer Service","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Transfer Service"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","locale":"en"},"1485":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#configuration-boundary","content":"Configuration Boundary","locale":"en"},"1486":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#choose-a-state-store","content":"Choose a State Store","locale":"en"},"1487":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#required-configuration","content":"Required Configuration","locale":"en"},"1488":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-3","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#deploy-and-verify","content":"Deploy and Verify","locale":"en"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-4","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#rollout-and-rollback","content":"Rollout and Rollback","locale":"en"},"1490":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-5","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","content":"Transfer is an independent service for Load and Export jobs. It persists job\nstate, plans work from mount and Worker information, dispatches tasks to\nWorkers, and receives task reports. It does not host a replica of the full\nCurvine metadata tree.","locale":"en"},"1491":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-6","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","content":"Deploy Transfer after the Master and Workers are healthy. It is optional: a\ncluster that does not enable Transfer continues to use the legacy Master Load\nand Export path.","locale":"en"},"1492":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-7","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#configuration-boundary","content":"The service and the client use different Transfer settings. Do not change the\nrunning Master or Worker configuration merely to deploy Transfer.","locale":"en"},"1493":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-8","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#configuration-boundary","content":"| Component        | Required change                                                                    | Notes                                                                                |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Transfer service | Set `transfer.enabled = true`, a persistent `store_url`, and a reachable endpoint. | The service configuration must also contain the existing cluster's Master addresses. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1494":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-9","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#configuration-boundary","content":"| Component         | Required change                                         | Notes                                                                                          |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| CLI or SDK client | Set `transfer.enabled = true` and `transfer.endpoints`. | `cv load`, `cv export`, and compatible status/cancel commands then use Transfer automatically. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1495":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-10","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#configuration-boundary","content":"| Component | Required change                                     | Notes                                                                |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Master    | None. Keep Transfer disabled during staged rollout. | Enabling it makes the Master reject the legacy Load and Export RPCs. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1496":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-11","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#configuration-boundary","content":"| Component | Required change | Notes                                                                                            |\n| --------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Worker    | None.           | Workers need a version that supports Transfer tasks. Report endpoints are included in each task. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1497":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-12","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#configuration-boundary","content":"The client configuration contains no database URL. The store belongs only to\nthe Transfer service.","locale":"en"},"1498":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-13","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#choose-a-state-store","content":"| Store  | Topology                                               | Use it when                                               |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| SQLite | One Transfer instance and one persistent local volume. | Evaluation, development, or a single-instance deployment. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1499":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-14","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#choose-a-state-store","content":"| Store | Topology                                             | Use it when                                                |\n| ----- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| MySQL | Two or more Transfer instances sharing one database. | Production high availability and rolling service upgrades. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1500":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-15","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#choose-a-state-store","content":"Never point multiple Transfer instances at independent SQLite files. They would\nhold different job state and cannot fail over correctly.","locale":"en"},"1501":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-16","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#required-configuration","content":"The Transfer server needs a complete cluster configuration, including\n`[client]` Master addresses. Add this section only to the Transfer server's\nconfiguration file:","locale":"en"},"1502":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-17","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#required-configuration","content":"For a MySQL-backed service, replace `store_url` with a shared MySQL URL. Do not\nput credentials in a client configuration file or a ConfigMap.","locale":"en"},"1503":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-18","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#required-configuration","content":"Clients need only the routing settings:","locale":"en"},"1504":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-19","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#required-configuration","content":"If `endpoints` is omitted, Curvine derives one endpoint from\n`hostname:rpc_port`. Explicit endpoints are recommended for Kubernetes and for\nany address that differs from the bind address.","locale":"en"},"1505":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-20","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#deploy-and-verify","content":"Deploy on bare metal","locale":"en"},"1506":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-21","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#deploy-and-verify","content":"Deploy on Kubernetes","locale":"en"},"1507":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-22","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#deploy-and-verify","content":"Transfer configuration reference","locale":"en"},"1508":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-23","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#deploy-and-verify","content":"After deployment, run `cv transfer list` from a client configured for Transfer.\nSubmit a small mounted UFS file with `cv load <path> --watch`, then verify that\nthe job reaches `Completed` and the target can be read with `cv fs --cache-only get`.","locale":"en"},"1509":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview-24","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service/Overview#rollout-and-rollback","content":"Enable Transfer in clients gradually. A client with `transfer.enabled = false`\ncontinues to use the legacy Master job API, so deploying the service alone does\nnot change existing workloads. To roll back a client, disable Transfer in that\nclient configuration; do not delete a Transfer store while jobs are active.","locale":"en"},"1510":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service","type":"page","content":"Transfer Service","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Transfer Service"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Transfer-Service","locale":"en"},"1511":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions","type":"page","content":"Build Instructions","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions","locale":"en"},"1512":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"1513":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions#build-steps-linux---ubuntudebian-example","content":"Build Steps (Linux - Ubuntu/Debian example)","locale":"en"},"1514":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/build-instructions","type":"heading