id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"Common Configuration","locale":"en"},"1928":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","content":"Curvine provides multi-language SDKs so applications can access the Curvine filesystem via RPC (metadata from Master, block data from Workers) without using FUSE or the S3 gateway.","locale":"en"},"1929":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-6","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK      | Crate / Package                     | Use Case                                   |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Rust** | `curvine-client` / `curvine-libsdk` | Native Rust applications, high performance |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1930":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-7","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK      | Crate / Package                                                         | Use Case                                      |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| **Java** | Hadoop-compatible FileSystem (`fs.cv://`), Java SDK from curvine-libsdk | Hadoop/Spark/Flink and other JVM applications |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1931":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-8","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK        | Crate / Package                     | Use Case                   |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| **Python** | Python bindings from curvine-libsdk | ML/data pipelines, scripts |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1932":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-9","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"All SDKs require a running Curvine cluster (Master and Workers) and correct client configuration (e.g. `master_addrs` in `curvine-cluster.toml` or equivalent).","locale":"en"},"1933":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-10","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#rust-sdk","content":"Use the `curvine-client` crate (or the Rust API exposed by `curvine-libsdk`) to create files, read/write data, and list directories programmatically. Configuration is typically loaded from `curvine-cluster.toml` or via environment variables.","locale":"en"},"1934":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#rust-sdk","content":"For build and usage, see the Development Guide and the Curvine source repository (e.g. `curvine-client`, `curvine-libsdk`, and integration tests under `curvine-tests`).","locale":"en"},"1935":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-12","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-sdk","content":"**Hadoop FileSystem**: Configure `fs.cv.impl` and `fs.cv.master_addrs` in `core-site.xml` or `curvine-site.xml` so that `FileSystem.get(URI.create(\"curvine:///path\"), conf)` uses Curvine. See Deployment Preparation for `fs.cv.master_addrs`.","locale":"en"},"1936":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-13","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-sdk","content":"**Java API**: Use the Curvine Java SDK from curvine-libsdk for direct RPC access when not using the Hadoop FileSystem interface.","locale":"en"},"1937":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-14","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-sdk","content":"Compatible with Hadoop, Spark, Flink, and other JVM-based frameworks that support custom FileSystem implementations.","locale":"en"},"1938":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-15","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"The Python SDK (from curvine-libsdk) provides a native API to read/write files and list directories on Curvine. Typical use cases include ML training, data preprocessing, and automation scripts.","locale":"en"},"1939":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-16","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"For installation and examples, see the Curvine source repository and Development Guide.","locale":"en"},"1940":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-17","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"**Master address**: Set `client.master_addrs` in the cluster config (e.g. `curvine-cluster.toml`) or pass the equivalent in each SDK (e.g. Java `fs.cv.master_addrs`). Format: `host1:8995,host2:8995`.","locale":"en"},"1941":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-18","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"**Config file**: Most SDKs accept a config file path (e.g. `conf/curvine-cluster.toml`). The same file is used by the CLI (`cv`), FUSE, and S3 gateway.","locale":"en"},"1942":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-19","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"For UFS (unified file system) access, mount UFS paths with `cv mount`; then SDK operations on the corresponding Curvine paths will follow the same semantics as Data Orchestration.","locale":"en"},"1943":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"page","content":"Dynamic PVC In Deployment","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","K8S CSI Driver"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","locale":"en"},"1944":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#example-topology","content":"Example Topology","locale":"en"},"1945":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#storageclass-parameters","content":"StorageClass Parameters","locale":"en"},"1946":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#apply-the-example","content":"Apply The Example","locale":"en"},"1947":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#what-the-example-creates","content":"What The Example Creates","locale":"en"},"1948":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#shared-pvc","content":"Shared PVC","locale":"en"},"1949":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#deployment","content":"Deployment","locale":"en"},"1950":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deploy