on, where missing `fs-path` is replaced with `/` before `mount-key` generation.","locale":"en"},"2045":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-57","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-subpath","content":"`NodePublishVolume` in `pkg/csi/node.go` computes the host subpath differently depending on the mounted root:","locale":"en"},"2046":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-58","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-subpath","content":"If `fs-path == /`, the host subpath is `mnt-path + curvine-path`","locale":"en"},"2047":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-59","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-subpath","content":"If `fs-path != /`, the host subpath is `mnt-path + relative(curvine-path, fs-path)`","locale":"en"},"2048":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-60","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-subpath","content":"Examples from the implementation comments:","locale":"en"},"2049":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-61","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-subpath","content":"This is why multiple PVCs can share one FUSE process while still landing in different directories.","locale":"en"},"2050":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-62","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Dr