n","content":"`--mnt-number`","locale":"en"},"2073":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-85","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#fuse-command-construction","content":"The validator also still accepts several older keys such as `auto-cache`, `kernel-cache`, `master-hostname`, `master-rpc-port`, and `master-web-port`. Those keys are not separately documented on the current `curvine-fuse` CLI page, so treat them as compatibility behavior rather than a stable public contract.","locale":"en"},"2074":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-86","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#lifecycle-summary","content":"The controller validates StorageClass parameters and creates `curvine-path`.","locale":"en"},"2075":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-87","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#lifecycle-summary","content":"The controller returns `VolumeContext` containing `master-addrs`, `fs-path`, and `curvine-path`.","locale":"en"},"2076":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-88","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#lifecycle-summary","content":"The node plugin computes `cluster-id`, `mount-key`, and `mnt-path`.","locale":"en"},"2077":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-89","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#lifecycle-summary","content":"If a compatible FUSE process already exists for that `master-addrs + fs-path` pair, the node reuses it.","locale":"en"},"2078":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-90","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#lifecycle-summary","content":"Otherwise, the node starts a new `curvine-fuse` process.","locale":"en"},"2079":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-91","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#lifecycle-summary","content":"The node bind-mounts the correct subdirectory into the pod.","locale":"en"},"2080":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-92","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#lifecycle-summary","content":"When reference count reaches zero, `NodeUnstageVolume` stops the unused FUSE mount.","locale":"en"},"2081":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-93","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#static-versus-dynamic-pvs","content":"| Mode                         | Required attributes                                      | Controller behavior                         | Node behavior                                                 |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Dynamic PVC via StorageClass | `master-addrs`, optional `fs-path`, optional `path-type` | Generates `volumeHandle` and `curvine-path` | Mounts `fs-path`, then bind-mounts the generated subdirectory |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2082":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-94","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#static-versus-dynamic-pvs","content":"| Mode      | Required attributes            | Controller behavior        