--------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `-H, --human-readable` | Print human-readable sizes. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2540":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-80","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option                     | Description                                |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `-q, --hide-non-printable` | Replace non-printable characters with `?`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2541":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-81","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option            | Description       |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- |\n| `-R, --recursive` | List recursively. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2542":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-82","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option          | Description         |\n| --------------- | ------------------- |\n| `-r, --reverse` | Reverse sort order. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2543":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-83","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option        | Description                |\n| ------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `-t, --mtime` | Sort by modification time. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2544":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-84","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option       | Description   |\n| ------------ | ------------- |\n| `-S, --size` | Sort by size. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2545":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-85","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option        | Description                              |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `-u, --atime` | Use access time for display and sorting. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2546":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-86","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"| Option              | Description          |\n| ------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `-l, --long-format` | Long listing format. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2547":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-87","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#3-fs-file-system-operations","content":"In the current source, recursive mode for `chmod` / `chown` is exposed as the third positional argument `[RECURSIVE]`, not as a `--recursive` flag. Permission strings support octal values such as `755` / `0o755` and symbolic forms such as `u=rwx,g=rx,o=rx`. `chown` supports `user:group`, `user:`, and `:group`.","locale":"en"},"2548":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-88","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"The current implementation uses `mount` for three related workflows:","locale":"en"},"2549":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-89","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`cv mount`: list all mount points","locale":"en"},"2550":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-90","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`cv mount --check`: list mount points and validate UFS reachability","locale":"en"},"2551":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-91","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`cv mount <UFS_PATH> <CV_PATH> [OPTIONS]`: create or update a mount","locale":"en"},"2552":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-92","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`cv mount resync <CV_PATH> [OPTIONS]`: run metadata resync for an `fs_mode` mount","locale":"en"},"2553":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-93","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"Common options:","locale":"en"},"2554":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-94","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                 | Description                               |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `--config <key=value>` | UFS configuration entry. Can be repeated. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2555":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-95","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option     | Description                             |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `--update` | Update an existing mount configuration. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2556":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-96","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                               | Description                                                                           |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--check-path-consist <true\\|false>` | Whether to enforce path consistency between `UFS_PATH` and `CV_PATH`. Default `true`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2557":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-97","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option              | Description                                              |\n| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--read-verify-ufs` | Validate cached reads against UFS using `mtime` / `len`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2558":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-98","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                | Description                                                  |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--ttl-ms <DURATION>` | TTL, default `7d`. Supports durations such as `1h` and `7d`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2559":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-99","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option           | Description             |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `--replicas <N>` | Override replica count. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2560":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-100","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                | Description                               |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `--block-size <SIZE>` | Override block size, for example `128MB`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2561":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-101","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                      | Description            |\n| --------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `-s, --storage-type <TYPE>` | Override storage type. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2562":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-102","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                               | Description                                                               |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--write-type <cache_mode\\|fs_mode>` | The current source only distinguishes these two modes. Default `fs_mode`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2563":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-103","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option                                 | Description                             |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `--provider <auto\\|oss-hdfs\\|opendal>` | Select the UFS provider implementation. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2564":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-104","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option    | Description                                                     |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--check` | Only meaningful when listing mounts; also validates each entry. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2565":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-105","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option      | Description                                                                  |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `--dry-run` | During `resync`, scan and print differences without delete / create changes. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2566":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-106","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Option      | Description                                    |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `--verbose` | During `resync`, print detailed per-file logs. |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2567":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-107","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"**About `--provider`**: some URI schemes can map to multiple implementations. For example, `oss://...` may be handled either by OSS-HDFS / JindoSDK or by OpenDAL, so `--provider` lets you force the implementation.","locale":"en"},"2568":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-108","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Value  | Description                                         | Typical protocols     |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `auto` | Auto-select implementation based on the URI scheme. | All supported schemes |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"2569":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-109","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Value      | Description                            | Typical protocols |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `oss-hdfs` | Use JindoSDK / OSS-HDFS path handling. | `oss://`          |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"2570":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-110","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"| Value     | Description                 | Typical protocols                                                                 |\n| --------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `opendal` | Use OpenDAL-based backends. | `s3://`, `oss://`, `hdfs://`, `webhdfs://`, `cos://`, `gcs://`, `azblob://`, etc. |","locale":"en","table":"table-7"},"2571":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-111","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"There are also a few implementation details worth calling out:","locale":"en"},"2572":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-112","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For `s3://...` paths, if `s3.bucket_name` is not provided explicitly, the CLI auto-fills it from the URI.","locale":"en"},"2573":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-113","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For `hdfs://...` paths, if `hdfs.namenode` / `hdfs.root` are not provided explicitly, the CLI derives them from the URI.","locale":"en"},"2574":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-114","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"If the config contains `hdfs.kerberos.*` keys but neither `hdfs.kerberos.ccache` nor the `KRB5CCNAME` environment variable is present, the CLI prints a Kerberos ticket-cache warning.","locale":"en"},"2575":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-115","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`validate_path_and_configs` currently applies extra path validation only to S3 paths; other schemes mostly rely on later provider initialization and connectivity checks.","locale":"en"},"2576":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-116","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2577":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-117","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"For detailed parameter lists of each UFS type (S3, OSS, HDFS, WebHDFS), see Appendix: UFS Mount Parameters at the end.","locale":"en"},"2578":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-118","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"`--check-path-consist=true` is enabled by default. That means a path such as `s3://bucket/datasets` is normally expected to mount to `/bucket/datasets`. If you really need a different mapping, pass `--check-path-consist=false` explicitly.","locale":"en"},"2579":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-119","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#4-mount-mount-ufs-into-curvine","content":"In the current source, the first creation of an `fs_mode` mount automatically triggers a `resync`. Manual `cv mount resync ...` only works for `fs_mode` mount points.","locale":"en"},"2580":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-120","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#5-umount-remove-a-mount","content":"**Usage:** `cv umount <CURVINE_PATH>`","locale":"en"},"2581":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-121","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#5-umount-remove-a-mount","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2582":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-122","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"**Usage:** `cv load [OPTIONS] <SOURCE_PATH> [TARGET_PATH]`","locale":"en"},"2583":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-123","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                               |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `<SOURCE_PATH>`   | UFS source URI or a Curvine path below an existing mount. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"2584":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-124","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                                           |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[TARGET_PATH]`   | Optional Curvine destination. A mounted source path derives its target automatically. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"2585":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-125","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                    |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch`     | Watch job status immediately after submission. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"2586":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-126","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                   |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `--no-overwrite`  | Fail instead of replacing an existing target. |","locale":"en","table":"table-8"},"2587":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-127","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2588":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-128","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#6-load-submit-a-load-job","content":"With Transfer enabled, `load` submits a Transfer job. Otherwise it uses the\nlegacy Master job path. The command prints a job ID and target path in either\nmode.","locale":"en"},"2589":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-129","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"The command line does not change when standalone Transfer is enabled:","locale":"en"},"2590":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-130","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"| Client configuration         | `cv load` / `cv export` route                       |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[transfer] enabled = false` | Legacy Master Load API, for backward compatibility. |","locale":"en","table":"table-9"},"2591":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-131","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"| Client configuration        | `cv load` / `cv export` route                       |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[transfer] enabled = true` | Transfer service RPC, selected directly by the CLI. |","locale":"en","table":"table-9"},"2592":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-132","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#transfer-routing","content":"The Transfer service and the client must both be configured for Transfer. Master\nand Worker configuration does not change for a client-side rollout. A client\nwith `transfer.enabled = false` continues to submit through the legacy Master\nAPI.","locale":"en"},"2593":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-133","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"**Usage:** `cv export [OPTIONS] <PATH>`","locale":"en"},"2594":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-134","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"`<PATH>` must be a Curvine path below a mount. Curvine infers the UFS target\nfrom that mount.","locale":"en"},"2595":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-135","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                    |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `<PATH>`          | Curvine source path to export. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"2596":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-136","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                    |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch`     | Watch job status immediately after submission. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"2597":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-137","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                              |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `--no-overwrite`  | Fail when the UFS target already exists. |","locale":"en","table":"table-10"},"2598":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-138","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#7-export-export-a-curvine-path-to-ufs","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2599":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-139","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"**Usage:** `cv load-status [OPTIONS] <JOB_ID>`","locale":"en"},"2600":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-140","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description          |\n| ----------------- | -------------------- |\n| `<JOB_ID>`        | Load job identifier. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"2601":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-141","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description     |\n| ----------------- | --------------- |\n| `-v, --verbose`   | Verbose output. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"2602":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-142","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument        | Description                                                                 |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `-w, --watch <INTERVAL>` | Poll interval, default `5s`. Supports formats such as `1s`, `1m`, and `1h`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"2603":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-143","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--conf <PATH>`   | Optional one-command config override; normal use does not need it. |","locale":"en","table":"table-11"},"2604":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-144","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2605":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-145","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#8-load-status-query-job-status","content":"In the current implementation, `load-status` enters watch mode by default with a `5s` refresh interval. The source does not currently expose a dedicated one-shot status-only switch.","locale":"en"},"2606":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-146","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"**Usage:** `cv cancel-load [OPTIONS] <JOB_ID>`","locale":"en"},"2607":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-147","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description               |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `<JOB_ID>`        | Job identifier to cancel. |","locale":"en","table":"table-12"},"2608":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-148","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"| Option / Argument | Description                                                        |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `--conf <PATH>`   | Optional one-command config override; normal use does not need it. |","locale":"en","table":"table-12"},"2609":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-149","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#9-cancel-load-cancel-a-load-job","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2610":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-150","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"`cv transfer` is available only when `[transfer] enabled = true`. It is the\noperations command for listing, inspecting, retrying, and paging Transfer jobs;\nnormal submission remains `cv load` or `cv export`.","locale":"en"},"2611":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-151","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"It requires a reachable Transfer endpoint in the client configuration. See\nTransfer Service for deployment.","locale":"en"},"2612":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-152","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command            | Description                                                                            |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer list` | List jobs. Filter with `--kind load\\|export`, `--state`, `--tenant`, or `--submitter`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2613":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-153","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                       | Description                                                                       |\n| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer status <JOB_ID>` | Show one job. Add `--verbose` for task detail or `--watch --interval 1s` to poll. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2614":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-154","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                      | Description                   |\n| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer tasks <JOB_ID>` | Show a task page for one job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2615":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-155","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                       | Description            |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `cv transfer cancel <JOB_ID>` | Cancel a Transfer job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2616":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-156","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command                      | Description                                                         |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer retry <JOB_ID>` | Retry a failed, canceled, or partially successful job as a new job. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2617":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-157","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"| Command               | Description               |\n| --------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `cv transfer tenants` | Summarize jobs by tenant. |","locale":"en","table":"table-13"},"2618":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-158","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2619":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-159","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#10-transfer-operate-transfer-jobs","content":"`load-status` and `cancel-load` remain compatible shortcuts. With Transfer\nenabled, they call Transfer; with Transfer disabled, they call the legacy\nMaster implementation.","locale":"en"},"2620":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-160","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-version-show-version","content":"**Usage:** `cv version`","locale":"en"},"2621":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-161","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-version-show-version","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2622":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-162","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-version-show-version","content":"The current implementation prints `curvine-cli <version>` together with commit / branch information.","locale":"en"},"2623":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-163","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#11-version-show-version","content":"Every binary also accepts the global `--version-json` flag to print its full\nstructured version (component, release version, git provenance, protocol\nversion, capabilities) as JSON — see\nVersion Management and Compatibility:","locale":"en"},"2624":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-164","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`bin/dfs` in the distribution is a compatibility wrapper:","locale":"en"},"2625":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-165","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"When the first subcommand is `fs` or `report`, it calls Java `io.curvine.CurvineShell`.","locale":"en"},"2626":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-166","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`dfs fs` keeps Hadoop `FsShell` syntax, so subcommands look like `-ls`, `-mkdir`, `-rm -r` with single-dash command names.","locale":"en"},"2627":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-167","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Other subcommands are eventually forwarded to the Rust `curvine-cli`, but for normal operations `cv` is still the recommended entry point.","locale":"en"},"2628":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-168","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Examples:","locale":"en"},"2629":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-169","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"`dfs report info` is the Java-compat text-summary variant; conceptually it is close to `cv report all`, but the command name is different.","locale":"en"},"2630":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-170","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#compatibility-cli-dfs","content":"Use `dfs` when you need Hadoop shell compatibility or rely on Hadoop configuration files such as `core-site.xml` / `hdfs-site.xml`. Use `cv` when you want the full Curvine-native command set from current source.","locale":"en"},"2631":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-171","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Curvine also exposes a FUSE file system interface. After mounting it, for example via `bin/curvine-fuse.sh start`, you can operate on the mount point with normal Linux tools:","locale":"en"},"2632":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-172","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Typical categories:","locale":"en"},"2633":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-173","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Basic file operations: `ls`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm`, `mkdir`","locale":"en"},"2634":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-174","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Content inspection: `cat`, `grep`, `sed`","locale":"en"},"2635":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-175","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"File system information: `df -h`, `du -sh`, `stat`","locale":"en"},"2636":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-176","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"Permissions: `chmod`, `chown`","locale":"en"},"2637":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-177","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#posix--fuse","content":"If your goal is POSIX compatibility with existing tools, prefer FUSE. If you need Curvine-native mount, load, or node-management features, use `cv`.","locale":"en"},"2638":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-178","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#appendix-ufs-mount-parameters","content":"The following are common parameters passed through `--config key=value` when using `cv mount`. `Required` means it normally must be provided; `Optional` means it can be omitted if a default exists or if the CLI can infer it from the mount URI.","locale":"en"},"2639":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-179","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"Used with `--provider opendal` or auto-selection.","locale":"en"},"2640":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-180","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter         | Required/Optional | Description                                                       |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `s3.endpoint_url` | Required          | S3 service endpoint URL; must start with `http://` or `https://`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"2641":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-181","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter               | Required/Optional | Description    |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- | -------------- |\n| `s3.credentials.access` | Required          | Access Key ID. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"2642":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-182","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli#s3-s3-s3a","content":"| Parameter               | Required/Optional | Description        |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------ |\n| `s3.credentials.secret` | Required          | Secret Access Key. |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"2643":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli-183","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/cli","tags":[],"